			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'0','zoysia'=>'1'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Spring under all this tree canopy?','answer'=>'For 90%+ of established Spring lots — Spring Trails, Klein-area estates, Old Town Spring — Palmetto St. Augustine is the call. It handles the 4–5 hours of filtered light most established Spring lots actually get under mature oak and pine canopy. Bermuda fails almost universally under Spring canopy; we steer homeowners away from it on the front-edge estimate. On full-sun Augusta Pines and Gleannloch Farms lots we sometimes install Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda, and we step up to Zeon Zoysia on premium pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does my Spring lawn keep thinning out under my trees?','answer'=>'Three reasons working together: insufficient light reaching the turf (your canopy has grown over years and your lawn has been losing light gradually), surface tree roots competing with grass roots for water and nutrients, and accumulated leaf litter driving soil pH down. The fix is the whole package: limb up the lower 8–10 feet of canopy, prune surface tree roots, amend pH, and install the right shade-tolerant variety. We include all of that in our standard Spring canopy-lot install.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you work with Gleannloch Farms and Augusta Pines architectural review?','answer'=>'Yes — we have cleared the architectural-review process at both communities multiple times. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Gleannloch Farms and Augusta Pines proposal so the homeowner has the paperwork ready for the review board. We are familiar with the specific grass-variety standards and the timing windows these communities enforce.'),
				array('question'=>'Do I need different soil amendment in Augusta Pines than in Spring Trails?','answer'=>'Yes — and this is one of the most common mistakes other contractors make in Spring. Augusta Pines and Gleannloch Farms sit on sandier loam that benefits from organic amendment (compost-heavy) to hold moisture and nutrients. Spring Trails and Klein-area estates sit on a transitional profile under heavy canopy that benefits from sandy loam topsoil amendment plus pH correction. We calibrate the amendment to your specific soil test, not a generic Spring spec.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you install Klein ISD athletic fields and school-campus turf?','answer'=>'Yes — Klein ISD and Spring-area school athletic fields are a distinct part of our Spring book. We deliver laser-graded Tifway 419 Bermuda athletic fields with construction-grade base prep, irrigation coordination, grow-in protocols, and bid-document submittal packages. We also handle frontage, courtyard, and visible-entry sod for Spring-area schools, churches, and faith campuses.'),
				array('question'=>'Can you handle acreage and equestrian properties along FM 2920?','answer'=>'Constantly — FM 2920 corridor acreage is a meaningful part of our Spring book. These properties almost always pencil out as hybrid sod-plus-hydroseed plans: premium St. Augustine sod near the home, barn surrounds, and paddock perimeters; engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across pasture and outer-fence-line acreage. Equestrian properties get grazing-safe Bermuda seed blends across turn-out zones.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Spring install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Spring residential installs complete in 1–3 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots. Heavy-canopy installs in Spring Trails and Klein-area estates can add 1–2 days for canopy limb-up and root pruning. Acreage hybrid projects on the FM 2920 corridor typically take 5–10 working days. Athletic-field installs are project-scheduled with the school district and typically span 2–4 weeks including grow-in.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Spring sod install cost?','answer'=>'Spring sod pricing varies based on which Spring sub-market your lot sits in, the amount of canopy work required, soil amendment specs, grass variety, and project size. As a reference: typical Spring residential front-yard re-sods range from $3,000 on smaller Klein-area properties to $7,500+ on larger Augusta Pines and Gleannloch Farms lots. Full-yard quarter-acre installs typically run $5,500 to $13,000. Acreage hybrid plans on FM 2920 corridor properties typically run $12,000 to $40,000+. We provide line-item pricing on every Spring proposal.'),
			),
