				'lawn_challenges' => array('Mixed soil profiles','Shaded mature-tree lots','Drainage near creeks'),
				'we_install_in' => array(
					array('title'=>'Gleannloch Farms','content'=>'Premium master-planned community on sandier loam with mature canopy and a strict architectural-review process. Most installs here are Palmetto St. Augustine over an organic-amended surface, with Zeon Zoysia upgrades on pool-adjacent and signature front-yard zones. The HOA modification request paperwork ships with every Gleannloch quote.'),
					array('title'=>'Augusta Pines','content'=>'Golf-community estates with sandy loam soil and partial canopy — soil that drains faster than most of Spring, which means shorter and more frequent irrigation cycles during establishment. Bermuda actually works on the full-sun open-fairway-adjacent lots; St. Augustine dominates the canopy zones. Premium Zoysia common around pools.'),
					array('title'=>'Spring Trails','content'=>'Established residential with heavy oak and pine canopy and 40+ years of accumulated leaf litter driving soil pH downward. Almost every Spring Trails install we touch needs canopy limb-up, surface-root pruning, and pH-amended soil before sod goes down. Palmetto St. Augustine dominates; Bermuda fails reliably here.'),
					array('title'=>'Klein-area estates','content'=>'Spring\'s premium older estate corridor — large lots, mature tree canopy, and homeowners who want a country-club finish. We default to Palmetto St. Augustine on the family-lawn zones and Zeon Zoysia on architectural and pool-adjacent zones. Soil amendment depth runs to the high end of our normal Spring range.'),
					array('title'=>'Old Town Spring & adjacent older sections','content'=>'Smaller older lots with variable soil from a century of mixed use and some construction-fill contamination from periodic remodels. We soil-test every Old Town Spring lot before quoting amendment depth; the lot-to-lot variability is wider here than in newer Spring sub-markets.'),
