			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'0','zoysia'=>'1'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does everyone in Fulshear recommend a hybrid sod-plus-hydroseed install?','answer'=>'Because Fulshear lot sizes are dramatically larger than the Houston-metro suburban average — most properties run from a half-acre custom-build lot to 5-acre estate lots to 10-acre acreage tracts. Full-sod installs on properties at this scale almost never pencil out financially; homeowners who try anyway typically spend two to three times what a hybrid plan would cost for marginal additional appearance benefit. Hybrid plans put premium sod where the eye actually lands and engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across back acreage, saving 40–60% versus full sod while delivering nearly identical visible appearance.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Cross Creek Ranch approve my re-sod or new install?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match the community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled Cross Creek Ranch modification request package with every proposal so the homeowner has the paperwork ready for the review board. We have cleared review at Cross Creek Ranch many times over the past several years, and Palmetto St. Augustine is the most-approved variety on visible front and side yards.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Fulshear?','answer'=>'On established lots with partial canopy (Cross Creek Ranch, Fulbrook, Weston Lakes), Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the filtered light, tolerates Fulshear soil once installed over an amended surface, and clears Cross Creek Ranch architectural review without friction. On full-sun newer-construction lots (newer Cross Creek Ranch filings, Tamarron, FM 1463 corridor), Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs. Hydroseed zones in hybrid plans use engineered Bermuda blends.'),
				array('question'=>'Do I really need different soil amendment in different parts of my Fulshear lot?','answer'=>'Yes — and this is one of the most common mistakes other contractors make in Fulshear. Soil variability across a single Fulshear lot is wide enough that one zone might need 2 inches of sandy loam amendment while another zone 50 feet away needs 3 inches of organic-heavy amendment with pH correction. We dig 3–5 soil probes across every Fulshear lot before quoting and calibrate amendment specs to each zone — not a generic Fulshear spec.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do equestrian properties along FM 359 and FM 1463?','answer'=>'Constantly — equestrian acreage along the FM 359 and FM 1463 corridors is one of our most active Fulshear segments. These properties almost always pencil out as hybrid plans: premium St. Augustine sod near the home, barn surrounds, paddock perimeters, and turn-out gates; engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across pasture and outer-fence-line acreage with grazing-safe seed blends (no toxic species). We coordinate with fence contractors and barn builders on sequencing.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle SWPPP-permitted commercial work and detention pond stabilization?','answer'=>'Yes — Fulshear commercial work and SWPPP-permitted erosion-control on detention ponds is a meaningful part of our commercial book. We deliver bonded fiber matrix hydromulch with erosion-control blanket overlay on detention pond banks, coordinate directly with civil engineers and municipal inspectors, and ship full bid-document submittal packages with every commercial proposal. We are bondable and insured to Fulshear commercial standards.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Fulshear hybrid install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most half-acre to 2-acre Fulshear hybrid projects complete in 4–8 working days, weather permitting. Larger 5-acre to 10-acre estate hybrid projects run 2–4 weeks depending on prep, drainage, and coordination with adjacent trades (builder, irrigation, fencing). The sod component installs in 1–3 days; the hydroseed component completes in 1–2 days; the rest is prep, grading, drainage, and clean-up across multiple zones.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Fulshear install cost?','answer'=>'Fulshear pricing varies based on lot size, the sod-to-hydroseed ratio, soil zone variability, and HOA documentation requirements. As a reference: typical Fulshear front-yard re-sods on Cross Creek Ranch and Tamarron lots range from $3,500 to $7,500. Full-yard quarter-acre to half-acre Cross Creek Ranch and Fulbrook installs typically run $7,000 to $16,000. Acreage hybrid plans on 1-acre to 5-acre Weston Lakes and Fulbrook estate lots typically run $18,000 to $55,000+. Larger 10+ acre FM 359 corridor plans are quoted as custom estate bids. We provide line-item pricing on every Fulshear proposal.'),
