			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'0','zoysia'=>'1'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does Magnolia need both moisture-retention amendment AND pH correction?','answer'=>'Because Magnolia sits on sandy loam (which drains fast and needs moisture-retention amendment) layered with mature pine and hardwood canopy on most established lots (which drives soil pH downward through decades of needle and leaf litter). The combination is unique. Compost-heavy organic amendment alone (without pH correction) leaves the lawn struggling under acidic soil. pH correction alone (without moisture amendment) leaves the lawn drying out in sandy soil. We do both as standard scope on established Magnolia lots with canopy.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Magnolia?','answer'=>'On established Magnolia lots under mature canopy (High Meadow Ranch, Mostyn Manor, Magnolia Ridge, Westwood), Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the 4–5 hours of filtered light, tolerates Magnolia sandy loam over a properly amended and pH-corrected surface, and clears HOA architectural review at all major Magnolia communities. On full-sun Magnolia acreage, Tifway 419 Bermuda for sod zones and Bermuda hydroseed blends for outer acreage. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do acreage and hybrid plans on FM 1488 and FM 1774?','answer'=>'Constantly — FM 1488 and FM 1774 acreage is one of our most active Magnolia segments. These properties almost always pencil out as hybrid plans: premium sod near the home, pool, and barn surrounds; engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across pasture and outer-fence-line acreage with grazing-safe seed blends on equestrian properties.'),
				array('question'=>'Will High Meadow Ranch, Mostyn Manor, Magnolia Ridge, or Westwood approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every High Meadow Ranch, Mostyn Manor, Magnolia Ridge, and Westwood proposal. We have cleared review at each of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do equestrian and ranch installs in Magnolia?','answer'=>'Yes — equestrian properties are a meaningful segment of our Magnolia acreage book. We coordinate with fence contractors and barn builders, install premium St. Augustine or Zoysia sod near the home, barn surrounds, and paddock perimeters, and apply Bermuda hydroseed with grazing-safe (non-toxic) seed blends across pasture.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does new builder sod fail under mature Magnolia canopy?','answer'=>'Because production builders typically install Raleigh St. Augustine over raw sandy loam under mature canopy with no organic amendment, no pH correction, and no canopy limb-up. It looks great on closing day and fails within 18 months as the combination of fast-draining soil, acidic pH, and limited filtered light overwhelms the variety. We correct this pattern with the full Magnolia canopy-lot scope.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Magnolia install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Magnolia residential installs complete in 1–3 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots. Heavy-canopy installs add 1–2 days for canopy limb-up and root pruning. Acreage hybrid plans on 1-acre to 5-acre properties typically take 5–10 working days. Larger 10+ acre equestrian hybrid installs can take 2–4 weeks depending on scope.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Magnolia sod install cost?','answer'=>'Magnolia sod pricing varies based on lot size, canopy work, and hybrid scope. As a reference: typical Magnolia residential front-yard re-sods range from $2,800 to $6,500. Full-yard quarter-acre to half-acre installs typically run $5,500 to $13,000. Acreage hybrid plans on 1-acre to 5-acre FM 1488 and FM 1774 properties typically run $13,000 to $35,000+. Larger 10+ acre equestrian hybrid installs typically run $25,000 to $75,000+.'),
			),
