			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why is The Livable Forest such a hard market for lawns?','answer'=>'Because 50+ years of mature pine and hardwood canopy across Kings Forest, Forest Cove, Kings River, Bear Branch, and Kingwood Greens have created install constraints that most contractors do not specialize in. Filtered light averages 3–4 hours per day on many established lots. Decades of pine-needle and leaf litter have driven soil pH below 5.5 on most established Kingwood installs. Surface tree feeder roots compete aggressively with new sod. Every Kingwood install requires canopy limb-up, surface-root pruning, pH-corrected organic amendment, and shade-tolerant variety selection.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Kingwood?','answer'=>'Palmetto St. Augustine on roughly 95% of established Kingwood lots — it handles the 3–4 hours of filtered light, tolerates Kingwood acidic pH once corrected with lime amendment, and clears Kingwood Service Association architectural review at all major villages. On the deepest-shade pockets we install Sapphire St. Augustine. Bermuda fails almost universally under Kingwood canopy; we steer homeowners away from it. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs in Kingwood Greens estate filings.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does pH amendment matter so much in Kingwood?','answer'=>'Because 50+ years of accumulated pine-needle and leaf litter under most Kingwood lots has driven soil pH well below the 6.0–7.0 range St. Augustine prefers. We routinely measure pH below 5.5 on established Kingwood installs. Acidic pH locks up nutrients and prevents healthy root development. We soil-test every Kingwood install and add lime to correct pH where the test indicates it. This step is non-negotiable on most established Kingwood lots.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle Harvey, Imelda, and Beryl flood recovery in Kings Forest and Forest Cove?','answer'=>'Yes — flood recovery is a meaningful recurring part of our Kingwood book. After every major flood event we restore Kings Forest, Forest Cove, and West Fork-adjacent lawns with drainage redesign, elevation review, French drain installation, and salt-flush amendment on the worst-affected lots. We coordinate with insurance adjusters on documented claims and with civil-engineering firms on the larger drainage redesigns.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Kings Forest, Forest Cove, Kings River, Bear Branch, or Kingwood Greens approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each village\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled Kingwood Service Association modification request package with every Kingwood proposal. We have cleared review at each Kingwood village multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'Do I really need surface-root pruning on a Kingwood install?','answer'=>'Yes — and it is the step contractors most commonly skip. Mature pine and hardwood feeder roots radiate within 4–6 inches of the soil surface for 40+ feet of horizontal range from the trunk. New sod laid over those feeder roots is in immediate competition for water and nutrients on day one. Without surface-root pruning, even shade-tolerant Palmetto St. Augustine struggles within two seasons. We include this step in standard scope on every established Kingwood lot.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Kingwood install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Kingwood residential installs complete in 2–4 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots — the canopy limb-up and pH amendment work adds 1–2 days vs. a non-canopy install. Flood-recovery installs with drainage redesign typically take 5–10 working days depending on scope. Premium Kingwood Greens installs with Zeon Zoysia and integrated pool-and-patio scope typically take 3–5 days.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Kingwood sod install cost?','answer'=>'Kingwood sod pricing reflects the standard Kingwood install scope — canopy limb-up, surface-root pruning, pH-corrected amendment, and shade-tolerant variety are built into pricing. As a reference: typical Kingwood front-yard re-sods range from $3,500 to $7,500 depending on canopy density. Full-yard quarter-acre to half-acre installs typically run $7,000 to $16,000. Premium Kingwood Greens installs with Zeon Zoysia upgrades typically run $14,000 to $30,000+. Flood-recovery installs with drainage redesign typically run $10,000 to $25,000+.'),
			),
