			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does every Missouri City lawn need a soil amendment?','answer'=>'Because Missouri City sits on some of the most active expansive clay soil in the southwest Houston metro. The clay is denser, more impermeable, and more aggressive in its swell-and-shrink cycle than typical Houston gumbo. Sod laid directly on raw Missouri City clay cannot push roots into the surface — they bounce off and the lawn fails within 18–24 months. Every successful Missouri City install includes a 2–3 inch sandy loam topsoil amendment tilled into the upper layer of clay before sod goes down.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Sienna, Riverstone, First Colony, or Quail Valley approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Sienna, Riverstone, First Colony, and Quail Valley proposal so the homeowner has the paperwork ready for the review board. We have cleared review at each of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Missouri City?','answer'=>'On established Missouri City lots with partial canopy (most Sienna, First Colony, and Quail Valley filings), Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the filtered light, tolerates Missouri City expansive clay once installed over the proper amendment, and clears HOA architectural review at all major Missouri City communities. On full-sun newer-construction Sienna and Riverstone front yards we install Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does new builder sod keep dying in Sienna and Riverstone?','answer'=>'Because the production builder lays Raleigh St. Augustine directly over raw Missouri City expansive clay with no amendment layer and no drainage correction. It looks great on closing day and fails over the next 18–24 months as roots cannot penetrate the impermeable clay below. We correct this pattern dozens of times per year — strip, decompact, amend with 2–3 inches of sandy loam, regrade, and reinstall with Palmetto St. Augustine.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle drainage issues common in Missouri City back yards?','answer'=>'Yes — and on most Missouri City lots, drainage correction is built into standard scope rather than treated as an upcharge. We regrade for 2% minimum slope away from the home foundation as part of every install. On lots that hold water, we install French drains, channel drains, or catch basins tied into existing storm-water infrastructure. Drainage is essential on Missouri City expansive clay.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do canopy work on Quail Valley golf-community lots?','answer'=>'Yes — Quail Valley golf-community installs require pre-install canopy limb-up, surface-root pruning, and pH amendment on top of the standard expansive-clay amendment scope. Mature pecan and oak canopy in Quail Valley creates the same install constraints we see in The Woodlands and Spring; we include canopy work in standard scope on every Quail Valley canopy-lot proposal.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Missouri City install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Missouri City residential installs complete in 2–4 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots because of the soil-amendment component — the amendment work adds 1 day vs. a non-amended install. Quail Valley canopy-lot installs can add another 1–2 days for canopy limb-up. Premium pool-adjacent installs with Zeon Zoysia typically take 3–5 days.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Missouri City sod install cost?','answer'=>'Missouri City sod pricing is driven primarily by soil amendment scope (non-negotiable) and HOA documentation. As a reference: typical Missouri City front-yard re-sods with full clay amendment range from $3,500 to $7,000. Full-yard quarter-acre installs typically run $6,500 to $14,000. Premium Quail Valley golf-community installs with canopy work and Zeon Zoysia typically run $9,000 to $20,000+. Every Missouri City proposal includes line-item pricing for amendment, drainage, grass, install labor, and HOA paperwork.'),
			),
