			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why is Rosenberg soil so variable across a single property?','answer'=>'Because Rosenberg sits along the Brazos River corridor where centuries of river deposition created a layered, non-uniform soil profile. Sandy loam in one part of a lot can transition to clay-influenced loam 30 feet away. We dig 3–5 soil probes across every Rosenberg lot before quoting and calibrate amendment to each zone — not a generic Rosenberg spec.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Rosenberg?','answer'=>'On established Rosenberg lots with partial canopy (Walnut Creek, Summer Lakes, older sections), Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the filtered light most established lots get and tolerates river-influenced soil over an amended surface. On full-sun newer-construction Seabourne Creek and adjacent filings, Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Seabourne Creek, Walnut Creek, or Summer Lakes approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Seabourne Creek, Walnut Creek, and Summer Lakes proposal. We have cleared review at each of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle floodplain and drainage compliance on Brazos-adjacent properties?','answer'=>'Yes — and on lower-elevation Rosenberg lots, drainage compliance is the entire conversation before grass varieties. We review existing storm-water plans, coordinate elevation with civil-engineering documentation, install French drains tied into existing infrastructure, and apply flood-tolerant Palmetto St. Augustine selection on the most-affected lots.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do acreage and equestrian installs along FM 762 and toward Beasley?','answer'=>'Constantly — FM 762 corridor acreage is one of our most active Rosenberg segments. These properties almost always pencil out as hybrid plans: premium St. Augustine sod near the home, barn surrounds, paddock perimeters, and turn-out gates; engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across pasture and outer-fence-line acreage with grazing-safe seed blends (no toxic species).'),
				array('question'=>'Do I need topsoil amendment on a Rosenberg install?','answer'=>'Almost always, and the amendment composition will vary across the lot rather than being uniform. Sandier zones benefit from organic amendment to hold moisture and nutrients. Clay-influenced zones benefit from sandy loam amendment to improve drainage. We soil-test every Rosenberg lot and calibrate amendment to each zone.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Rosenberg install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Rosenberg residential installs complete in 1–3 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots. Floodplain-adjacent installs with French drain work can add 1–2 days. Acreage hybrid projects on FM 762 corridor properties typically take 5–10 working days depending on prep and the sod-to-hydroseed ratio.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Rosenberg sod install cost?','answer'=>'Rosenberg sod pricing varies based on soil mapping, floodplain proximity, canopy work, and project size. As a reference: typical Rosenberg front-yard re-sods on Seabourne Creek, Walnut Creek, and Summer Lakes lots range from $2,700 to $6,500. Full-yard quarter-acre installs typically run $5,000 to $12,000. Acreage hybrid plans on FM 762 corridor properties typically run $13,000 to $40,000+. We provide line-item pricing on every Rosenberg proposal.'),
			),
