			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does every Pasadena lawn need aggressive decompaction?','answer'=>'Because Pasadena sits on heavy coastal clay that has been compressed by decades of industrial-equipment traffic, periodic flooding, and construction activity. The compaction layer is dramatically denser than typical Houston gumbo. Sod laid directly on raw compacted Pasadena clay cannot push roots into the surface — they bounce off and the lawn fails within 18–24 months. Every successful Pasadena install starts with aggressive till-out of the compaction layer to 4–6 inches followed by 2–3 inch sandy loam amendment.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does new builder sod keep dying in Strawberry Park and Genoa?','answer'=>'Because the production builder lays Raleigh St. Augustine directly over raw decades-compacted Pasadena clay with no amendment layer and no aggressive decompaction. It looks great on closing day and fails over the next 18–24 months as roots cannot penetrate the dense compaction below. We correct this pattern dozens of times per year — aggressive till-out, 2–3 inch sandy loam amendment, regrade, and reinstall with Palmetto St. Augustine.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Pasadena?','answer'=>'On 85%+ of Pasadena lots, Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the partial canopy most established Pasadena lots have, tolerates the coastal-clay water profile once installed over a properly decompacted and amended surface, and clears any applicable HOA architectural review. On full-sun newer Genoa-area lots with corrected drainage and amendment we occasionally install Tifway 419 Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs where the prep is done right.'),
				array('question'=>'Are there industrial-adjacent soil-quality considerations I should know about?','answer'=>'On most Pasadena lots, no — standard decompaction and amendment scope handles everything. On the rare lots where soil testing surfaces contamination concerns (typically lots very close to past industrial activity), we recommend additional remediation including soil replacement rather than amendment, and quote that work transparently as a separate line item with documentation. We soil-test every Pasadena lot before quoting so the homeowner knows exactly what they are dealing with.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do commercial and industrial work along Beltway 8 and SH-225?','answer'=>'Yes — Pasadena commercial and industrial work is a meaningful segment of our Pasadena book. We deliver hybrid sod-plus-hydroseed installs along Beltway 8 retail corridors, TXDOT-spec hydroseed blends on SH-225 industrial pads, and bonded fiber matrix erosion control on permitted construction sites. We carry refinery-adjacent insurance coverage and ship full bid-document submittal packages with every commercial Pasadena proposal.'),
				array('question'=>'Can you handle the drainage issues common in Pasadena back yards?','answer'=>'Yes — and on most Pasadena lots, drainage correction is built into standard scope rather than treated as an upcharge. We regrade for 2% minimum slope away from the foundation as part of every install. On lots that hold water, we install French drains, channel drains, or catch basins tied into existing storm-water infrastructure. On Armand Bayou-adjacent lots we coordinate with civil-engineering firms on larger floodplain corrections.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Pasadena install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Pasadena residential installs complete in 2–4 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots because of the aggressive decompaction component — the decompaction work adds 1 day vs. a standard install. Standard installs without aggressive decompaction needs complete in 1–2 days. Commercial Beltway 8 corridor installs are scheduled to the GC calendar and typically span 1–3 weeks depending on scope.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Pasadena sod install cost?','answer'=>'Pasadena sod pricing is driven primarily by aggressive decompaction and amendment scope. As a reference: typical Pasadena front-yard re-sods with full decompaction and amendment range from $3,000 to $6,500. Full-yard quarter-acre Pasadena installs typically run $5,500 to $12,500. Pool-and-patio installs typically run $8,000 to $18,000. Commercial Beltway 8 corridor projects are quoted as custom bids with SWPPP compliance and refinery-adjacent insurance. Every Pasadena proposal includes line-item pricing.'),
