			'name' => 'Pearland', 'slug' => 'pearland-tx',
			'fields' => array(
				'short_heading' => 'Pearland',
				'heading_text' => 'Sod Installation & Grass Establishment in Pearland, TX',
				'short_description_listing_view' => 'Shadow Creek Ranch to Silverlake, Pearland is one of our highest-density service areas.',
				'short_description' => 'Shadow Creek Ranch to Silverlake, Pearland is one of our highest-density service areas.',
				'tagline' => '"Sod where appearance matters most. Hydroseeding where scale matters most."',
				'installation_done' => '410+ installed · Since 2016',
				'lawn_establishment_heading' => 'Premium sod & lawn establishment for Pearland, TX properties',
				'lawn_establishment_sub_heading' => 'Whether you\'re a homeowner upgrading the front yard, a builder finishing a custom home, or an HOA restoring entry-feature lawns — GrassHouston brings the right mix of sod, hydroseeding, and hybrid solutions to Pearland, Texas.',
				'lawn_establishment_content' => 'Pearland sits on some of the most expansive clay soil in Greater Houston, and that single fact drives nearly every install decision we make here. The clay holds water for days after rain, cracks open in summer drought, and physically lifts and drops anything resting on it as it swells and contracts through the year. Sod installed directly on raw Pearland clay — which is what most production builders do — will look beautiful on closing day and fail within two seasons.

Our standard Pearland install includes a soil shovel test on the front-edge inspection, a topsoil amendment layer of 2–3 inches of sandy loam tilled into the surface, and a documented drainage plan that pulls water away from the home foundation at 2% minimum slope. Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona all show the same patterns; we plan for them by default.

We have completed multi-lot builder closeout programs across Pearland (most recently a 42-lot St. Augustine closeout scheduled to the builder\'s closing calendar), and we handle HOA common-area work for several master-planned communities here. The same soil-first, drainage-first discipline applies whether the project is one home or forty.

Recommended grass for Pearland: St. Augustine, Bermuda · Soil profile: Pearland\'s clay-heavy subgrades require careful drainage planning and soil amendment — we plan for it on every install.',
				'deep_dive_heading' => 'What makes Pearland lawn installation different',
				'deep_dive_content' => 'Pearland, Texas is the lawn installation market where expansive clay is the entire conversation. Where Houston gumbo clay is bad, Pearland clay is worse — denser, more expansive, more aggressive in its swell-and-shrink cycle through the seasons. The clay holds water for days after rain, cracks open inches wide in summer drought, and physically lifts and drops anything resting on it as it expands and contracts. Sod installed directly on raw Pearland clay — which is exactly what production builders do across Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona — will look beautiful on closing day and fail within 18–24 months. Roughly 410 of our installs since 2016 have been in Pearland, and the failure pattern is so consistent we now design our Pearland install scope around it by default.

the soil-amendment non-negotiable.

Pearland production-builder closeout work is a meaningful and consistent piece of our commercial book. We have completed multi-lot final-grade sod programs across Shadow Creek Ranch and adjacent master-planned community filings — the most recent being a 42-lot St. Augustine closeout scheduled to the builder\'s closing calendar over a six-week window. Builder closeout work in Pearland requires not just the install discipline but also the scheduling discipline to coordinate with the GC superintendent, the irrigation contractor, the fencing crew, and the closing calendar. We are bonded and insured to Pearland commercial standards, and we ship submittal packages with every multi-lot proposal.

Pearland HOA architectural review and common-area work is the third meaningful segment. Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona all enforce specific grass-variety standards and require modification request paperwork for any visible-from-the-street turf replacement. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Pearland proposal where review applies. On the common-area side, we handle entry monument restoration, median re-sod, and amenity-center lawn work for multiple Pearland HOAs and property-management firms — with predictable scheduling, coastal-clay-spec drainage standards, and property-manager-friendly billing.',
				'grass_installation_conetent' => '<p class="text-stone-600 mb-5 leading-relaxed">Pearland\'s clay-heavy subgrades require careful drainage planning and soil amendment — we plan for it on every install.</p>

<ul class="space-y-3 mb-6">
