			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does every Pearland lawn need a soil amendment?','answer'=>'Because Pearland sits on some of the most expansive clay soil in Greater Houston. The clay is denser, more impermeable, and more aggressive in its swell-and-shrink cycle than typical Houston gumbo. Sod laid directly on raw Pearland clay cannot push roots into the surface — they bounce off the impermeable clay and the lawn fails within 18–24 months. Every successful Pearland install includes a 2–3 inch sandy loam topsoil amendment tilled into the upper layer of clay before sod goes down. This step is the entire difference between a 10-year Pearland lawn and a 2-year Pearland lawn.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does new builder sod keep dying in Shadow Creek Ranch and Silverlake?','answer'=>'Because the production builder lays Raleigh St. Augustine directly over raw Pearland clay with no amendment layer, no drainage correction, and no soil prep beyond cosmetic surface scraping. It looks great on closing day and fails over the next 18–24 months as roots cannot penetrate the impermeable clay below. We correct this exact pattern dozens of times per year in Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona — strip, decompact, amend with 2–3 inches of sandy loam, regrade, and reinstall.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Shadow Creek Ranch (or Silverlake / Pomona) approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match the community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona proposal so the homeowner has the paperwork ready for the review board. We have cleared review at every one of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Pearland?','answer'=>'On established Pearland lots with partial canopy and family-lawn use, Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the partial shade most established Pearland lots have, tolerates Pearland clay once installed over the proper amendment layer, and clears HOA architectural review at Shadow Creek Ranch, Silverlake, Southern Trails, and Pomona. On full-sun newer-construction front yards we install Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs where the amendment is done right.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle drainage issues common in Pearland back yards?','answer'=>'Yes — and on most Pearland lots, drainage correction is built into standard scope rather than treated as an upcharge. We regrade for 2% minimum slope away from the home foundation as part of every install. On lots that hold water (low spots that pond, back fence lines that channel runoff toward the slab, side yards with poor drainage), we install French drains, channel drains, or catch basins tied into existing storm-water infrastructure. Drainage is essential on Pearland expansive clay.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do multi-lot Pearland builder closeout programs?','answer'=>'Yes — multi-lot final-grade sod installs for production and custom builders across Shadow Creek Ranch and other Pearland subdivision filings are a meaningful part of our Pearland commercial book. Our most recent 42-lot St. Augustine closeout is one of several. We schedule against the builder\'s closing calendar, coordinate with the builder superintendent on staging and access, and ship submittal packages that match the bid documents. Insurance certificates and bondability documentation accompany every commercial Pearland proposal.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Pearland install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Pearland residential installs complete in 2–4 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots because of the soil-amendment component — the amendment work adds 1 day vs. a non-amended install. Builder closeout multi-lot programs are scheduled to the closing calendar across a 4–8 week window. Premium pool-adjacent installs with Zeon Zoysia and integrated drainage typically take 3–5 days.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Pearland sod install cost?','answer'=>'Pearland sod pricing is driven primarily by soil amendment scope (non-negotiable) and drainage corrections. As a reference: typical Pearland front-yard re-sods with full clay amendment range from $3,500 to $7,000. Full-yard quarter-acre Pearland installs typically run $6,500 to $14,000. Premium Zeon Zoysia upgrades on pool-and-patio installs typically run $9,000 to $20,000+. Multi-lot builder closeout programs are quoted as bundled commitments. Every Pearland proposal includes line-item pricing for amendment, drainage, grass, install labor, and HOA paperwork.'),
			),
			'meta' => array(
				'residential' => array(
					array('heading'=>'Shadow Creek Ranch & master-planned-community homeowners','content'=>'Architectural-review-cleared sod installs over expansive Pearland clay with non-negotiable soil amendment, drainage corrections, and pre-filled Shadow Creek Ranch modification request paperwork. The bulk of our Pearland residential book.'),
					array('heading'=>'Silverlake, Southern Trails & Pomona homeowners','content'=>'Re-sod over expansive clay with 2–3 inch sandy loam amendment layer, drainage corrections at 2% minimum slope away from foundation, and grass-variety selection (typically Palmetto St. Augustine) that tolerates clay swell-and-shrink cycles. HOA paperwork included.'),
					array('heading'=>'New-construction Pearland homeowners replacing builder grass','content'=>'Pre-emptive re-sod over failing builder-installed sod on raw Pearland clay — strip the surface, till out compaction, add the 2–3 inch sandy loam amendment, regrade for drainage, and reinstall with the right variety. The lawn the builder should have given you.'),
					array('heading'=>'Pearland pool, patio & outdoor-living projects','content'=>'Premium Zeon Zoysia or Palmetto St. Augustine framing pool decks, outdoor kitchens, and patio surrounds on Pearland expansive-clay lots — coordinated with pool contractors on integrated drainage and waterproofing plans.'),
