			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does my Conroe lawn need different watering than my friend\'s Pearland lawn?','answer'=>'Because Conroe soil is dramatically different from Pearland soil. Conroe sits on sandy loam that drains faster than the expansive clay under Pearland or the prairie clay under Katy. Water passes through the root zone faster, which means shorter and more frequent watering cycles during establishment (and ongoing) compared to clay-soil neighbors. Our standard Conroe care calendar reflects this — typically 2–3 shorter cycles per day during the first week vs. 1–2 longer cycles on clay-soil installs.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Conroe?','answer'=>'On established Conroe lots under mature canopy (April Sound canopy zones, Bentwater interior estates, in-town older sections), Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the 4–5 hours of filtered light, tolerates Conroe sandy loam over an organic-amended surface, and recovers well from foot traffic. On full-sun newer construction lots (Grand Central Park, Graystone Hills, newer Lake Conroe filings), Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Do I really need different soil amendment in Conroe than in Pearland or Katy?','answer'=>'Yes — and this is one of the most common mistakes other contractors make in Conroe. Pearland and Katy installs typically need sandy loam amendment to improve drainage on clay subgrades. Conroe installs typically need compost-heavy organic amendment to improve moisture and nutrient retention on naturally fast-draining sandy loam. The amendment is different, the depth is different, and the long-term care calendar is different.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle Lake Conroe shoreline and slope stabilization?','answer'=>'Yes — Lake Conroe-adjacent shoreline and slope work is a meaningful part of our Conroe estate book. We coordinate bonded fiber matrix hydromulch, erosion-control blanket overlay, and retaining-wall-adjacent turf installation with our erosion-control crews on April Sound, Bentwater, and other lake-fronting estate properties. We coordinate with civil-engineering firms on documented elevation and drainage compliance where required.'),
				array('question'=>'Are there Lake Conroe-area irrigation restrictions I should know about?','answer'=>'Yes — Lake Conroe-area water-use regulations and varying well-water vs. municipal-water source availability create real planning constraints on Conroe estate installs. We document the irrigation water source and any applicable Lake Conroe-area restrictions on every estate estimate so the homeowner knows exactly what the first 30 days of establishment will require and how to plan around any seasonal restrictions.'),
				array('question'=>'Will April Sound, Bentwater, or Grand Central Park approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every April Sound, Bentwater, Grand Central Park, and Graystone Hills proposal. We have cleared review at each of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do industrial hydroseed and SWPPP-permitted commercial work on the I-45 north corridor?','answer'=>'Yes — this is one of our most active Conroe segments. We deliver TXDOT-spec hydroseed blends on industrial pads, bonded fiber matrix on slopes that need erosion control, and full SWPPP compliance coordinated with civil-engineering teams. Our 22-acre Conroe Industrial Site Hydroseed is the reference installation we cite on commercial bids across the I-45 north corridor.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Conroe sod install cost?','answer'=>'Conroe sod pricing varies by segment. As a reference: typical Conroe residential front-yard re-sods on Grand Central Park, Graystone Hills, and adjacent lots range from $2,800 to $6,500. Full-yard quarter-acre to half-acre residential installs typically run $5,500 to $13,000. Lake Conroe estate installs with shoreline stabilization typically run $12,000 to $35,000+. Acreage hybrid plans on FM 1097 and FM 105 corridor properties typically run $15,000 to $45,000+. Industrial hydroseed and SWPPP-permitted projects are quoted as custom commercial bids.'),
