			'name' => 'Cypress', 'slug' => 'cypress-tx',
			'fields' => array(
				'short_heading' => 'Cypress',
				'heading_text' => 'Sod Installation & Grass Establishment in Cypress, TX',
				'short_description_listing_view' => 'Bridgeland, Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, and Fairfield — Cypress is one of our highest-volume northwest Houston markets.',
				'short_description' => 'Bridgeland, Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, and Fairfield — Cypress is one of our highest-volume northwest Houston markets.',
				'tagline' => '"Sod where appearance matters most. Hydroseeding where scale matters most."',
				'installation_done' => '380+ installed · Since 2016',
				'lawn_establishment_heading' => 'Premium sod & lawn establishment for Cypress, TX properties',
				'lawn_establishment_sub_heading' => 'Whether you\'re a homeowner upgrading the front yard, a builder finishing a custom home, or an HOA restoring entry-feature lawns — GrassHouston brings the right mix of sod, hydroseeding, and hybrid solutions to Cypress, Texas.',
				'lawn_establishment_content' => 'Cypress sits on prairie-clay subgrades similar to Katy but with more drainage variability lot-to-lot because of the Cypress Creek watershed influence across much of the city. Bridgeland, Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, Fairfield, and Blackhorse Ranch all share these patterns: dense clay subgrades, new-construction compaction, and aging builder turf hitting its predictable failure curve.

Our standard Cypress install includes the 2–3 inch sandy loam topsoil amendment, drainage corrections at 2% minimum slope, and Palmetto St. Augustine or Tifway 419 Bermuda variety selection calibrated to canopy density and HOA standards.

Bridgeland is a master-planned community with strict architectural review enforcement. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Bridgeland proposal and have cleared review there many times. The same applies for Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, and Fairfield.

Recommended grass for Cypress: St. Augustine, Bermuda · Soil profile: Prairie clay with Cypress Creek watershed drainage variability — non-negotiable amendment and HOA paperwork on most installs.',
				'deep_dive_heading' => 'What makes Cypress lawn installation different',
				'deep_dive_content' => 'Cypress, Texas is one of our highest-volume northwest Houston lawn-installation markets and one of the most consistent in terms of the patterns we plan for. The defining geographic facts are the prairie-clay subgrades shared with neighboring Katy, the Cypress Creek watershed influence that creates drainage variability across much of the city, the dense concentration of master-planned-community architectural review across Bridgeland, Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, Fairfield, and Blackhorse Ranch, and the steady stream of new-construction work along the Grand Parkway / SH-99 corridor. Roughly 380 of our installs since 2016 have been in Cypress, and the standard scope is well-established.

the builder closeout cycle.

Cypress Creek watershed influence is the second defining factor. Lower-elevation Cypress properties along the creek and its tributaries — particularly older Fairfield filings, Norchester-adjacent sections, and Cypress Forest properties — see meaningful drainage variability lot-to-lot. We coordinate elevation review and French drain installation on flood-prone lots before recommending grass varieties, and we have a recurring storm-recovery book here from Harvey, Imelda, and recent events.

Bridgeland, Towne Lake, and Coles Crossing architectural review is the third defining Cypress factor. Each community enforces grass-variety standards on visible front and side yards and runs modification request processes for any turf replacement. We have cleared review at each multiple times and ship the paperwork with every proposal. Acreage Cypress along the FM 2920 corridor and toward Hockley/Waller is hybrid-turf country — premium sod near the home, engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across outer acreage.',
				'grass_installation_conetent' => '<p class="text-stone-600 mb-5 leading-relaxed">Prairie clay with Cypress Creek watershed drainage variability — non-negotiable amendment and HOA paperwork on most installs.</p>

