			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why does new builder sod keep dying in Bridgeland, Towne Lake, and Coles Crossing?','answer'=>'Because the production builder lays Raleigh St. Augustine directly over raw Cypress prairie clay with no amendment layer and no drainage correction. It looks great on closing day and fails within 12–24 months. We correct this pattern dozens of times per year — strip, decompact, amend with 2–3 inches of sandy loam, regrade, and reinstall with Palmetto St. Augustine.'),
				array('question'=>'Will Bridgeland, Towne Lake, Coles Crossing, Fairfield, or Blackhorse Ranch approve my re-sod?','answer'=>'Yes — provided the grass variety, install method, and timing match each community\'s architectural standards. We ship a pre-filled HOA modification request package with every Cypress proposal. We have cleared review at each of these communities multiple times.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Cypress?','answer'=>'On 80%+ of Cypress lots, Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the partial canopy most established Cypress lots have, tolerates Cypress prairie clay over a properly amended surface, and clears HOA architectural review across Cypress master-planned communities. On full-sun newer-construction front yards in Bridgeland and Towne Lake, Tifway 419 or TifTuf Bermuda. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs.'),
				array('question'=>'Do I need topsoil amendment on a Cypress install?','answer'=>'On almost every Cypress lot, yes. The prairie clay underneath your lot drains poorly, cracks in drought, and was compacted by heavy construction equipment. Our standard Cypress install adds 2–3 inches of sandy loam topsoil amendment tilled into the surface — non-negotiable.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle Cypress Creek flood recovery?','answer'=>'Yes — Cypress Creek-adjacent flood recovery is a meaningful recurring part of our Cypress book. We restore Fairfield, Norchester-adjacent, and Cypress Creek-fronting lawns with drainage redesign, elevation review, and French drain installation tied into existing storm-water infrastructure.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do acreage installs along FM 2920 toward Hockley?','answer'=>'Yes — FM 2920 corridor acreage is one of our most active Cypress segments. These properties almost always pencil out as hybrid plans: premium St. Augustine sod near the home, barn surrounds, and paddock perimeters; engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across pasture with grazing-safe seed blends on equestrian properties.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Cypress install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most Cypress residential installs complete in 2–4 working days on quarter-acre to half-acre lots. Acreage hybrid projects along FM 2920 typically take 5–10 working days. Cypress Creek-adjacent flood-recovery installs with drainage redesign typically take 5–10 working days.'),
				array('question'=>'What does a typical Cypress sod install cost?','answer'=>'Cypress sod pricing varies based on soil amendment, drainage, HOA documentation, and grass variety. As a reference: typical Cypress front-yard re-sods range from $3,200 to $7,000. Full-yard quarter-acre installs typically run $6,000 to $13,500. Acreage hybrid plans typically run $14,000 to $42,000+. Every Cypress proposal includes line-item pricing.'),
			),
