			'show' => array('st_augustine'=>'1','bermuda'=>'1','zoysia'=>'0'),
			'faqs' => array(
				array('question'=>'Why is hybrid sod-plus-hydroseed the right answer on most Hockley properties?','answer'=>'Because Hockley lot sizes are dramatically larger than the Houston-metro suburban average — most properties run from 1 acre to 100+ acres. Full-sod installs on properties at this scale almost never pencil out financially. Hybrid plans put premium sod where the eye actually lands (near the home, pool, barn surrounds, paddock perimeters) and engineered Bermuda hydroseeding across outer acreage and pasture, saving 50–70% versus full sod while delivering nearly identical visible appearance.'),
				array('question'=>'What grass works best in Hockley?','answer'=>'On established Hockley lots with partial canopy near the home, Palmetto St. Augustine — it handles the filtered light, tolerates Hockley sandy loam over an organic-amended surface, and recovers well from foot traffic in barn-surround and paddock-perimeter zones. On full-sun Hockley acreage and pasture, Tifway 419 Bermuda for sod zones and engineered Bermuda hydroseed blends for outer acreage. Premium Zeon Zoysia on pool-and-patio installs near the home.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do equestrian and FFA-property installs in Hockley?','answer'=>'Constantly — equestrian and FFA properties are one of our most active Hockley segments. We coordinate with fence contractors and barn builders, install premium St. Augustine or Zoysia sod near the home, barn surrounds, paddock perimeters, and turn-out gates, and apply Bermuda hydroseed with grazing-safe (non-toxic) seed blends across pasture. We never install toxic grass species on any property with livestock access.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you handle working ranch and hay-pasture hydroseed installs?','answer'=>'Yes — large-scale hydroseed installs on working ranches and commercial hay-pasture operations are a meaningful part of our Hockley book. We deliver custom Bermuda seed blends, grazing-safe specifications, and coordinated establishment timelines that account for grazing rotation. Bonded fiber matrix on slopes that need erosion control.'),
				array('question'=>'Why does Hockley need different soil amendment than Pearland or Sugar Land?','answer'=>'Because Hockley sits on sandy loam that drains dramatically faster than the expansive clay under Pearland, Sugar Land, or Katy. Pearland installs need sandy loam amendment to improve drainage on clay subgrades. Hockley installs need compost-heavy organic amendment to improve moisture and nutrient retention on naturally fast-draining sandy loam. The amendment is different, the depth is different, and the long-term care calendar is different.'),
				array('question'=>'How long does a Hockley hybrid install take to complete?','answer'=>'Most 1-acre to 2-acre Hockley hybrid projects complete in 3–7 working days, weather permitting. Larger 5-acre to 20+ acre estate and equestrian hybrid projects run 2–4 weeks depending on prep, fencing/barn coordination, and the sod-to-hydroseed ratio. The sod component installs in 1–3 days; the hydroseed component completes in 1–2 days; the rest is prep, grading, drainage, and clean-up across multiple zones.'),
				array('question'=>'Do you do FM 2920 commercial and industrial work in Hockley?','answer'=>'Yes — FM 2920 corridor commercial work is part of our Hockley book. We deliver TXDOT-spec hydroseed blends on industrial pads, bonded fiber matrix on slopes, and SWPPP compliance on permitted construction sites. We are bondable and insured, and we ship full bid-document submittal packages with every commercial Hockley proposal.'),
